<title>USA: Mich. $145 mln agency bonds repriced, yields cut.</title>
<headline>Mich. $145 mln agency bonds repriced, yields cut.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-01-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Goldman Sachs &amp; Co said Thursday it repriced State Building Authority of Michigan's $145 million bond deal, lowering yields in the 2009 and 2010 special sinking fund bonds.</p>
<p>The repricing follows:  </p>
<p>STATE BUILDING AUTHORITY</p>
<p>STATE OF MICHIGAN</p>
<p>RE: $144,790,000*</p>
<p>1997 REVENUE BONDS, SERIES I</p>
<p>VERBAL AWARD</p>
<p>NOTE REPRICING OF THE SUPER SINKERS IN 2009 AND 2010.</p>
<p>					    141,440,000*</p>
<p>					    SERIAL BONDS</p>
<p>  MOODY'S: A1		  S&amp;P: AA-		   FITCH: AA-</p>
